"_gp_margin_vs_hist":null,"_score_margin_vs_hist":null,"_gate_piotroski":7,"_gp_piotroski":true,"_score_piotroski":77.8,"_gate_spread":-0.0452303876414483,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.5148082092590825,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":14.2,"_gate_incr_roic":0.6131062059794538,"_gp_incr_roic":true,"_score_incr_roic":100.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.019273912815724867,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":26.9,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":0.007055255264338757,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":7.1,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.04051550858471839,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":56.1,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.00445812886878989,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":92.6,"_gate_insider_own":0.00511,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":3.4,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Smurfit Westrock Plc, together with its subsidiaries, manufactures, distributes, and sells containerboard, corrugated containers, and other paper-based packaging products in North America, South America, Europe, Asia, Africa, Australia, and internationally. The company produces containerboard and paperboard; packaging of corrugated containers; consumer packaging; and offers solid board, kraft paper, and graphic board, as well as other packaging products, such as solidboard packaging, paper sacks and bag-in-box. It produces linerboard and corrugated medium and paperboard; and other paper-based packaging, such as folding cartons, inserts, labels and displays. The company primarily serves food and beverage, healthcare, beauty and personal care, garden, consumer goods, industrial, and foodservice markets. It markets its products through its own sales force, independent sales representatives, and independent distributors. Smurfit Westrock Plc was founded in 1934 and is headquartered in Dublin, Ireland.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Anthony Paul J. Smurfit | President, Group CEO & Director | Age 62 | Compensation: $4.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 96K people. Revenue per employee of $325K ranks in the below the sector median among Consumer Cyclical peers. Each employee generates $12K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $1K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 15\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Smurfit WestRock plc is a large-cap consumer cyclical business with a $22.2B market cap on $31.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +48% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 3% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 20% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $1.2B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 4 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 4.85\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin 2.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 4.1% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.5) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.3% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 56/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; durably derated by the market \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 71% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 25% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Growing faster than most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"INVESTOR ALERT: Pomerantz Law Firm Investigates Claims On Behalf of Investors of Smurfit Westrock plc - SW","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/investor-alert-pomerantz-law-firm-investigates-claims-on-behalf-of-investors-of-smurfit-westrock-plc---sw-302937489.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794497400.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.447,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["legal"]},{"title":"Xinhua Silk Road: Wuliangye explores new paradigm for global branding at panda-themed conference in SW China","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/xinhua-silk-road-wuliangye-explores-new-paradigm-for-global-branding-at-panda-themed-conference-in-sw-china-302932852.html","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794192300.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"(SW) Risk Channels and Responsive Allocation","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/10/SW_Risk_Channels_and_Responsive_Allocation_110826024001_1794123601.html","date":"2026-11-08","timestamp":1794123601.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.202,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Smurfit Westrock (NYSE:SW) Stock Price Breaks Above 200 Day Moving Average on Analyst Downgrade","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/05/smurfit-westrock-nysesw-stock-price-breaks-above-200-day-moving-average-on-analyst-downgrade.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793856068.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.772,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"Smurfit Westrock (SW) Could Be 20% Undervalued After Q3 Results And Dividend Reaffirmation","source":"s